course: dictionary
lesson: 15638
title: Words that end things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A terminator is something that ends or destroys something. The word has several meanings, so the clues around it tell you which one you need. «The pest terminator came on Tuesday to check the kitchen for mice.» The clue is pest. A terminator is someone who gets rid of pests.
explain: In space, the terminator is the line on the Moon where day turns to night. Through a telescope, craters near this line look sharpest. «Through the telescope, the terminator on the Moon looked sharp.» The clues are telescope and Moon, so this is a line in space, not a robot.
explain: Some meanings come from films and tech. The Terminator is a famous robot from films that started in 1984, so people joke that a tough, unstoppable person is a terminator. A cable terminator is a small part that closes the end of a cable or line.
fact: A terminator is something or someone that ends or destroys something.
fact: On the Moon or a planet, the terminator is the line that divides the day side from the night side.
fact: The Terminator is a famous action film robot, and people use the word for a tough, unstoppable robot or person.
fact: A terminator can also be a part that marks or closes the end of a cable, line or piece of data.
fact: Check the clues around the word, such as Moon, pest or cable, to find which meaning it has.
exercise: «The pest terminator checked the shed for rats.» What is a pest terminator? | A large dog that barks | Someone who grows flowers | *Someone who gets rid of pests | A person who sells shoes
exercise: «Through the telescope, we could see the terminator on the Moon.» What is the terminator here? | A famous robot from a film | *The line where day turns to night | The end of a long rope | A planet with rings
exercise: Ella says a tough, unstoppable person can be called a terminator. What does the word mean in this joke? | *Something tough that cannot be stopped | A quiet, soft toy | A person who grows plants | A type of cable
test: «The cable terminator kept the wire from fraying at the end.» What does terminator mean here? | A kind of cloud | The line between day and night | *A part that closes the end of a cable | A robot from a film
test: In «The terminator on the Moon looked sharp», which word tells you this is about space? | *Moon | Looked | Terminator | Sharp
exam: «The lunar terminator is the curved line of shadow on the Moon.» Which meaning does terminator have here? | A cable end | A tough robot from a film | *The line between day and night on a planet | A pest-killer
